Relevant columns and how they will be used  
(reference to table `spider2-public-data.1000_genomes.variants`)  

• `reference_name` : chromosome identifier – filter on “17”.  
• `start`, `end` : genomic coordinates – filter on the interval 41 196 311‑41 277 499 and keep in result.  
• `reference_bases` : reference allele – keep in result.  
• `alternate_bases` : array of alternate alleles – keep in result, deduplicate.  
• `VT` : variant type – keep in result.  
• `call` : repeated STRUCT containing per‑sample genotypes – UNNEST to derive genotype counts.  
• `AF`, `AF1`, `AFR_AF`, `AMR_AF`, `ASN_AF`, `EUR_AF` : allele‑frequency summaries from the 1000 Genomes project – keep in result.  

